  "name": "Question 1",
  "problem": "The equation \n\n$$\n{x}^{2}+ax+b={x}^{2}+10x+24\n$$\n\nis true for all values of $x,$ where $a$ and $b$ are constants. What is the value of $a+b?$",
  "worked_solution": "Since the equation is true for all values of $x,$ the expressions on both sides must be exactly the same. That means the coefficients of the matching powers of $x$ must be equal.\n\nLet's compare the coefficients:\n\n- The coefficient of $x$ on the left-hand side is $a,$ and on the right-hand side it is $10.$ So, we have \n\n$$\na=10.\n$$\n\n- The constant term on the left-hand side is $b,$ and on the right-hand side it is $24.$ So, we have \n\n$$\nb=24.\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the sum:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a+b & =10+24 \\\\  & =34\\end{aligned}\n$$",
